Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(studio): branching dialog and menu stop offering
 what the deployment has no way to do

A deployment that runs its own control plane has no billing and clones the
parent database itself, so three things in the branching UI are wrong for it.

Create branch printed hosted prices for compute and disk and a tax notice
whatever the deployment: print them only when billing is enabled
(useIsFeatureEnabled billing:all).

Include data was disabled with a "Requires PITR" badge unless the project had
the point-in-time-recovery add-on. A deployment says it can clone through the
flag supaviseBranchClones (the same ConfigCat document that carries
allowDataBranching), and the switch is enabled with either.

The Create pull request item of a branch menu linked to github.com for any
branch that had a git branch, connected repository or not. It appears only
when the project has a GitHub connection, whose repository the row already
receives.
